    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0548" n="514" xml:id="pg514"/>

                <head>252. Telegram From the Secretary of State to the
                        Embassy in Bolivia<anchor n="1" xml:id="d252-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-06-14T19:47:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                                1955—7:47 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>210. Because proposed joint program includes reference most major problems of
                    mutual interest to Bolivian and US governments, Department believes your current
                    discussions this program provide appropriate occasion refer to US understanding
                    and hope that negotiations with former owners nationalized mines to fix amount
                    compensation are continuing satisfactorily. In your discretion you may state
                    that although this matter is not a part of joint program, US believes that
                    substantial progress on compensation problem would improve climate for foreign
                    investment in Bolivia, thereby contributing to overall program objectives.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
